The §24.2–§24.6 function families (obsolescent aliases, C23 narrowing
arithmetic, total-order/NaN-payload, reentrant gamma, complex log10) were
all implemented and tested earlier this session.  This closes out the
remaining non-code deliverables and marks the tasklist complete:

- §24.8 Documentation: 12 man3 pages (scalb, significand, drem, gamma,
  pow10, matherr, fadd [the 24-name narrowing family], totalorder,
  canonicalize, getpayload [get/set/sig payload], lgamma_r, clog10) plus
  49 `.so` redirect stubs for the family-member aliases, all mandoc-clean.
  ERRORS/RETURN VALUE were read from the implementations (e.g. the f-prefixed
  narrowing functions return double per <math.h>; totalorder raises no fp
  exceptions; scalb's ±Inf-n edges), with deprecation notes on the
  obsolescent pages.
- §24.1/§24.7 Link-completeness: tests/lib/m/unit/test_symbol_audit.c — a
  fixture that references every added symbol so the LINK is the test;
  reports 60/60 tasklist-24 symbols resolved.  Wired into the test Makefile.
- All 44 checklist items ticked.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
